<http://dbpedia.org/resource/STS-62> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "STS-62 was a Space Shuttle program mission flown aboard Space Shuttle Columbia. The primary payloads were the USMP-02 microgravity experiments package and the OAST-2 engineering and technology payload, both in the orbiter's cargo bay. The two-week mission also featured a number of biomedical experiments focusing on the effects of long duration spaceflight. The landing was chronicled by the 1994 Discovery Channel special about the Space Shuttle program and served as the show's opening. A C.F. Martin backpacker guitar was also flown aboard Columbia during the mission."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Flagstaff,_Arizona> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Flagstaff** ( [*FLAG-staf*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key%29) is a city in, and the [county seat](:County_seat) of, [Coconino County](:Coconino_County%2C_Arizona) in [northern Arizona](:Northern_Arizona), in the southwestern United States. In 2019, the city's estimated population was 75,038. Flagstaff's combined metropolitan area has an estimated population of 139,097.Flagstaff lies near the southwestern edge of the [Colorado Plateau](:Colorado_Plateau) and within the [San Francisco volcanic field](:San_Francisco_volcanic_field), along the western side of the largest contiguous [ponderosa pine](:Pinus_ponderosa) forest in the continental United States. The city sits at about 7,000 feet (2,100 m) and is next to [Mount Elden](:Mount_Elden), just south of the [San Francisco Peaks](:San_Francisco_Peaks), the highest mountain range in the state of Arizona. [Humphreys Peak](:Humphreys_Peak), the highest point in Arizona at 12,637 feet (3,852 m), is about 10 miles (16 km) north of Flagstaff in [Kachina Peaks Wilderness](:Kachina_Peaks_Wilderness). [The geology of the Flagstaff area](http://repository.azgs.az.gov/uri_gin/azgs/dlio/1540) includes abundant volcanic rocks associated with the San Francisco Volcanic Field that range in age from late [Miocene](:Miocene) to late [Holocene](:Holocene). It also includes exposed rock from the [Mesozoic](:Mesozoic) and [Paleozoic](:Paleozoic) eras, with [Moenkopi Formation](:Moenkopi_Formation) red sandstone having once been quarried in the city; many of the historic downtown buildings were constructed with it. The [Rio de Flag](:Rio_de_Flag) river runs through the city, but only flows in response to rain or snowmelt.Originally settled by the [pre-Columbian](:Pre-Columbian) native [Sinagua](:Sinagua) people, the area of Flagstaff has fertile land from volcanic ash after eruptions in the 11th century. It was first settled as the present-day city in 1876. Local businessmen lobbied for [Route 66](:U%2ES%2E_Route_66) to pass through the city, which it did, turning the local industry from lumber to tourism and developing [downtown Flagstaff](:Downtown_Flagstaff%2C_Arizona). In 1930, [Pluto](:Pluto) was discovered from Flagstaff. The city developed further through to the end of the 1960s, with various observatories also used to choose [Moon landing](:Moon_landing) sites for the [Apollo missions](:List_of_Apollo_missions). Through the 1970s and 1980s, downtown fell into disrepair, but was revitalized with a major cultural heritage project in the 1990s.The city remains an important distribution hub for companies such as [Nestlé Purina PetCare](:Nestl%C3%A9_Purina_PetCare), and is home to the [U.S. Naval Observatory Flagstaff Station](:United_States_Naval_Observatory_Flagstaff_Station), the [United States Geological Survey](:United_States_Geological_Survey) Flagstaff Station, and [Northern Arizona University](:Northern_Arizona_University). Flagstaff has a strong tourism sector, due to its proximity to [Grand Canyon National Park](:Grand_Canyon_National_Park), [Oak Creek Canyon](:Oak_Creek_Canyon), the [Arizona Snowbowl](:Arizona_Snowbowl), [Meteor Crater](:Meteor_Crater), and [Historic Route 66](:U%2ES%2E_Route_66_in_Arizona%23Historic_Route_66)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
