<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ukrainian_Soviet_Socialist_Republic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Ukrainian Soviet Socialist Republic (Ukrainian: Украї́нська Радя́нська Соціалісти́чна Респу́бліка, Ukrainska Radianska Sotsialistychna Respublika; Russian: Украи́нская Сове́тская Социалисти́ческая Респу́блика), abbreviated as the Ukrainian SSR, UkrSSR, or UkSSR, and also known as Soviet Ukraine, was one of the constituent republics of the Soviet Union from 1922 until 1991. In the anthem of the Ukrainian SSR, it was referred to simply as Ukraine. Under the Soviet one-party model, the Ukrainian SSR was governed by the Communist Party of the Soviet Union through its republican branch: the Communist Party of Ukraine."@en .
