<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Stephen_Thorne_(astronaut)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Stephen Douglas Thorne** (February 11, 1953 – May 24, 1986), ([Lt Cmdr](:Lieutenant_Commander_%28United_States%29), [USN](:United_States_Navy%29), was an American [naval officer](:United_States_Navy) and [aviator](:United_States_naval_aviator), [test pilot](:Test_pilot) and a [NASA](:NASA) [astronaut](:Astronaut) candidate.He was born on February 11, 1953, in [Frankfurt](:Frankfurt), [West Germany](:West_Germany), and graduated from the U.S. Naval Academy in 1975. He was a Navy [fighter pilot](:Fighter_pilot) from 1976 until he became a [test pilot](:Test_pilot) in 1981.He was accepted for NASA astronaut training in June 1985, but died in an airplane accident where he was a passenger on May 24, 1986.He was survived by his wife, Sue Lotz of [Staunton, Virginia](:Staunton%2C_Virginia). His interests included [baseball](:Baseball), [running](:Running), [reading](:Reading_%28process%29), and [general aviation](:General_aviation)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
