<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hero_of_the_Russian_Federation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Hero of the Russian Federation (Russian: Герой Российской Федерации, romanized: Geroy Rossiyskoy Federatsii), also unofficially Hero of Russia (Russian: Герой России, romanized: Geroy Rossii), is the highest honorary title of the Russian Federation. The title comes with a Gold Star medal, an insignia of honour that identifies recipients. The title was established in 1992 and, as of 2015, was awarded more than 970 times, of which more than 440 were posthumously."@en .
