<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Boris_Yegorov> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Boris Borisovich Yegorov** (Template:Lang-ru; 26 November 1937 – 12 September 1994) was a [Soviet](:Soviet_Union) [physician](:Physician)-[cosmonaut](:Astronaut) who became the first physician to make a space flight.Yegorov came from a medical background, with his father a prominent [heart surgeon](:Cardiac_surgery), and his mother an [ophthalmologist](:Ophthalmology). He also selected medicine as a career and graduated from the [First Moscow State Medical University](:First_Moscow_State_Medical_University) in 1961. During the course of his studies, he came into contact with [Yuri Gagarin](:Yuri_Gagarin)'s training and became interested in [space medicine](:Space_medicine).Yegorov earned his doctorate in medicine, with his specialization being in disorders of the [sense of balance](:Sense_of_balance).Yegorov was selected as a member of the multi-disciplinary team that flew on [Voskhod 1](:Voskhod_1). It has been suggested that his father's influence within the [Politburo](:Politburo) may have had some bearing on the selection. As a result of this space flight, Yegorov was awarded the title of the [Hero of the Soviet Union](:Hero_of_the_Soviet_Union) on October 19, 1964.He died from a heart attack in 1994."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
