<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Aeronautics> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Aeronautics is the science or art involved with the study, design, and manufacturing of air flight–capable machines, and the techniques of operating aircraft and rockets within the atmosphere. The British Royal Aeronautical Society identifies the aspects of \"aeronautical Art, Science and Engineering\" and \"The profession of Aeronautics (which expression includes Astronautics).\" A significant part of aeronautical science is a branch of dynamics called aerodynamics, which deals with the motion of air and the way that it interacts with objects in motion, such as an aircraft."@en .
