<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Abdul_Ahad_Momand> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Abdul Ahad Momand** (Template:Lang-ps; born 1959) is a [Afghan-German](:Afghans_in_Germany) and former [Afghan Air Force](:Afghan_Air_Force) [aviator](:Aviator) who became the first, and currently only, Afghan citizen to journey to outer space.He became one of [Soyuz TM-6](:Soyuz_TM-6) crew members and spent nine days aboard the [Mir](:Mir) [space station](:Space_station) in 1988 as an [Intercosmos](:Intercosmos) Research Cosmonaut. He holds many records as an Afghan Astronaut. During this mission, Abdul Ahad Momand was the first cosmonaut to speak the [Pashto](:Pashto) language after he made a telephone call to [Afghanistan](:Democratic_Republic_of_Afghanistan), making it the fifth language to be officially spoken in space. He became the first Afghan citizen and the [fourth Muslim to visit outer space](:List_of_Muslim_astronauts), after [Sultan bin Salman Al Saud](:Sultan_bin_Salman_Al_Saud), [Muhammed Faris](:Muhammed_Faris), and [Musa Manarov](:Musa_Manarov)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
