<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Moscow_State_University> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Moscow State University 'M. V. Lomonosov' (MSU; Russian: Московский государственный университет имени М. В. Ломоносова, sometimes abbreviated МГУ, MGU) is a public research university located in Moscow, Russia. It was founded in 1755 by Ivan Shuvalov and Mikhail Lomonosov, after whom it was renamed 'Lomonosov University' in 1940. Its rector is Viktor Sadovnichiy."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Deke_Slayton> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Donald Kent \"Deke\" Slayton (March 1, 1924 – June 13, 1993) was a United States Air Force pilot, aeronautical engineer, and test pilot who was selected as one of the original NASA Mercury Seven astronauts. He went on to become NASA's first Chief of the Astronaut Office and Director of Flight Crew Operations, responsible for NASA crew assignments. He died from a brain tumor on June 13, 1993, aged 69."@en .
