<http://dbpedia.org/resource/S._David_Griggs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Stanley David Griggs** (September 7, 1939 – June 17, 1989) was a [United States Navy](:United_States_Navy) officer and a [NASA](:NASA) astronaut. He is credited with conducting the first unscheduled [extra-vehicular activity](:Extra-vehicular_activity) of the space program during Space Shuttle mission [STS-51-D](:STS-51-D). Griggs was killed when the vintage [World War II](:World_War_II)-era training aircraft he was piloting – a [North American AT-6](:North_American_AT-6)D (registration N3931S) – crashed near [Earle, Arkansas](:Earle%2C_Arkansas)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
