<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dick_Scobee> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Francis Richard** **Scobee** (May 19, 1939 – January 28, 1986) was an American [pilot](:Aircraft_pilot), [engineer](:Engineer), and [astronaut](:Astronaut). He was [killed](:Space_Shuttle_Challenger_disaster) while he was commanding the [Space Shuttle *Challenger*](:Space_Shuttle_Challenger) in 1986, which suffered catastrophic [booster](:Booster_rocket) failure during launch of the [STS-51-L](:STS-51-L) mission.He held a [Bachelor of Science](:Bachelor_of_Science) degree in [Aerospace Engineering](:Aerospace_Engineering), graduating from the [University of Arizona](:University_of_Arizona) in 1965. He was a [reciprocating engine](:Reciprocating_engine) [mechanic](:Mechanic) for the United States Air Force and served as a [combat](:Combat) [aviator](:Aviator) in the [Vietnam War](:Vietnam_War).Selected for [NASA Astronaut Corps](:NASA_Astronaut_Corps) in January 1978, Scobee completed his training in August 1979. While awaiting his first [orbital spaceflight](:Orbital_spaceflight) mission, he served as an [instructor pilot](:Flight_instructor) for the Shuttle's [747 carrier aircraft](:Shuttle_Carrier_Aircraft). In April 1984, he piloted *Challenger* mission [STS-41-C](:STS-41-C), which successfully deployed one [satellite](:Satellite) and repaired another."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
