<http://dbpedia.org/resource/University_of_Arizona> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "[32°13′54″N 110°57′07″W﻿ / ﻿32.23167°N 110.95194°W﻿ / 32.23167; -110.95194](https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=University_of_Arizona&params=32_13_54_N_110_57_07_W_region:US_type:edu_source:dewiki)The **University of Arizona** (**Arizona**, **U of A**, **UArizona**, or **UA**) is a [public](:Public_university) [land-grant](:Land-grant_university) [research university](:Research_university) in [Tucson, Arizona](:Tucson%2C_Arizona). Founded in 1885 by the [13th Arizona Territorial Legislature](:13th_Arizona_Territorial_Legislature), it was the first university in the [Arizona Territory](:Arizona_Territory).The university is part of the [Association of American Universities](:Association_of_American_Universities) and the [Universities Research Association](:Universities_Research_Association). In the former, it is the only member from the state of Arizona. The university is [classified](:Carnegie_Classification_of_Institutions_of_Higher_Education) among \"R1: Doctoral Universities – Very High Research Activity\". The University of Arizona is one of three universities governed by the [Arizona Board of Regents](:Arizona_Board_of_Regents). As of 2021[[update]](//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=University_of_Arizona&action=edit), the university enrolled 49,471 students in 19 separate colleges/schools, including the [University of Arizona College of Medicine](:University_of_Arizona_College_of_Medicine) in Tucson and Phoenix and the [James E. Rogers College of Law](:James_E%2E_Rogers_College_of_Law), and is affiliated with two academic medical centers ([Banner – University Medical Center Tucson](:Banner_University_Medical_Center_Tucson) and [Banner – University Medical Center Phoenix](:Banner_%E2%80%93_University_Medical_Center_Phoenix%29). In 2021, University of Arizona acquired [Ashford University](:Ashford_University), a former for-profit college with more than 30,000 students and rebranded it as [The University of Arizona Global Campus](:The_University_of_Arizona_Global_Campus).Known as the [Arizona Wildcats](:Arizona_Wildcats) (often shortened to \"Cats\"), the UA's intercollegiate athletic teams are members of the [Pac-12 Conference](:Pac-12_Conference) of the [NCAA](:National_Collegiate_Athletic_Association). UA athletes have won national titles in several sports, most notably men's basketball, baseball, and softball. The official colors of the university and its athletic teams are [cardinal red](:Cardinal_%28color%29) and [navy blue](:Navy_blue)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
