<http://dbpedia.org/resource/STS-58> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "STS-58 was a NASA mission flown by Space Shuttle Columbia launched from Kennedy Space Center, Florida, on 18 October 1993. The missions was primarily devoted to experiments concerning the physiological effects in space. This was the first in-flight use of the \"Portable In-flight Landing Operations Trainer\" (PILOT) simulation software. It was also the last time Columbia would land at Edwards Air Force Base, California."@en .
