<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Thomas_David_Jones> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Thomas David Jones** (born January 22, 1955) is a former United States astronaut. He was selected to the astronaut corps in 1990 and completed four [Space Shuttle](:Space_Shuttle) flights before retiring in 2001. He flew on [STS-59](:STS-59) and [STS-68](:STS-68) in 1994, [STS-80](:STS-80) in 1996, and [STS-98](:STS-98) in 2001. His total mission time was 53 days 48 minutes. He works as a planetary scientist, space operations consultant, astronaut speaker, and author."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
