<http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Lake_Tahoe,_California> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**South Lake Tahoe** is the most populous city in [El Dorado County](:El_Dorado_County%2C_California), [California](:California), United States, in the [Sierra Nevada](:Sierra_Nevada). The city's population was 21,330 at the 2020 census, down from 21,403 at the 2010 census. The city, along the southern edge of [Lake Tahoe](:Lake_Tahoe), extends about 5 miles (8 km) west-southwest along [U.S. Route 50](:U%2ES%2E_Route_50_in_California), also known as Lake Tahoe Boulevard. The east end of the city, on the California–[Nevada](:Nevada) state line right next to the town of [Stateline, Nevada](:Stateline%2C_Nevada), is mainly geared towards tourism, with T-shirt shops, restaurants, hotels, and [Heavenly Mountain Resort](:Heavenly_Mountain_Resort) with the Nevada casinos just across the state line in Stateline. The western end of town is mainly residential, and clusters around \"The Y\", the X-shaped intersection of US 50, [State Route 89](:California_State_Route_89), and the continuation of Lake Tahoe Boulevard after it loses its federal highway designation."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
