<http://dbpedia.org/resource/University_of_Sydney> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **University of Sydney** (**USYD**), also known as **Sydney University**, or informally **Sydney Uni**, is a [public](:Public_university) [research university](:Research_university) located in [Sydney](:Sydney), [Australia](:Australia). Founded in 1850, it is the oldest university in Australia and is one of the country's six [sandstone universities](:Sandstone_universities). The university comprises eight academic faculties and university schools, through which it offers bachelor, master and doctoral degrees.The university consistently ranks highly both nationally and internationally. [QS World University Rankings](:QS_World_University_Rankings) ranked the university top 40 in the world. The university is also ranked first in Australia and fourth in the world for QS graduate employability. It is one of the first universities in the world to admit students solely on academic merit, and opened their doors to women on the same basis as men.Five [Nobel](:Nobel_Prize) and two [Crafoord](:Crafoord_Prize) laureates have been affiliated with the university as graduates and faculty. The university has educated eight [Australian prime ministers](:Prime_minister_of_Australia), including incumbent [Anthony Albanese](:Anthony_Albanese); two [governors-general of Australia](:Governor-General_of_Australia); thirteen [premiers of New South Wales](:Premier_of_New_South_Wales), including incumbent [Dominic Perrottet](:Dominic_Perrottet); 20 justices of the [High Court of Australia](:High_Court_of_Australia), including four [chief justices](:Chief_Justice_of_Australia). The university has produced 110 [Rhodes Scholars](:Rhodes_Scholarship) and 19 [Gates Scholars](:Gates_Cambridge_Scholarship).The University of Sydney is a member of the [Group of Eight](:Group_of_Eight_%28Australian_universities%29), [CEMS](:Global_Alliance_in_Management_Education), the [Association of Pacific Rim Universities](:Association_of_Pacific_Rim_Universities) and the [Association of Commonwealth Universities](:Association_of_Commonwealth_Universities)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
