<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Naval_flight_officer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A naval flight officer (NFO) is a commissioned officer in the United States Navy or United States Marine Corps who specializes in airborne weapons and sensor systems. NFOs are not pilots (naval aviators), but they may perform many \"co-pilot\" or \"mission specialist\" functions, depending on the type of aircraft. Until 1966, their duties were performed by both commissioned officer and senior enlisted naval aviation observers (NAO)."@en .
