<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Peterhouse,_Cambridge> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Peterhouse is the oldest constituent college of the University of Cambridge in England, founded in 1284 by Hugh de Balsham, Bishop of Ely. Today, Peterhouse has 254 undergraduates, 116 full-time graduate students and 54 fellows. It is quite often erroneously referred to as Peterhouse College, although the correct name is simply Peterhouse."@en .
