<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lodewijk_van_den_Berg> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Lodewijk van den Berg** (Template:IPA-nl; March 24, 1932 – October 16, 2022) was a Dutch-born American [chemical engineer](:Chemical_engineer). He studied [crystal growth](:Crystal_growth) and flew on a 1985 [Space Shuttle *Challenger*](:Space_Shuttle_Challenger) mission as a [payload specialist](:Payload_Specialist).Van den Berg was born in the [Netherlands](:Netherlands) and was an [astronaut](:Astronaut); he was a [naturalized](:Naturalization) American and not a Dutch citizen when he flew on the Challenger. He was married and had two children. He lived in Florida and worked as a chief scientist at the Constellation Technology Corporation."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
