<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Joe_Engle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Joe Henry Engle (born August 26, 1932) is an American pilot, aeronautical engineer and former NASA astronaut. He was the commander of two Space Shuttle missions including STS-2 in 1981, the program's second orbital flight. He also flew three flights in the Shuttle program's 1977 Approach and Landing Tests. Engle is one of twelve pilots who flew the North American X-15, an experimental spaceplane jointly operated by the Air Force and NASA. Engle is an experienced spaceplane operator and the last living X-15 pilot."@en .
