<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Fayetteville,_North_Carolina> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fayetteville (/ˈfeɪətˌvɪl, ˈfɛdvəl/) is a city in Cumberland County, North Carolina, United States. It is the county seat of Cumberland County, and is best known as the home of Fort Bragg, a major U.S. Army installation northwest of the city. Fayetteville has received the All-America City Award from the National Civic League three times. As of the 2020 census it had a population of 208,501, It is the 6th-largest city in North Carolina. Fayetteville is in the Sandhills in the western part of the Coastal Plain region, on the Cape Fear River."@en .
