<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kabul_Polytechnic_University> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Kabul Polytechnic University is the main center of educating engineers in Kabul, Afghanistan. It was founded on 13 October 1963 (1342 mizan in the Afghan calendar) as Kabul Polytechnic Institute and is located in 72 hectares of land in , north-western Kabul. In the opening ceremony government officials from both Afghanistan and other countries were present. Since its establishment it has been considered one of the important entities in providing education and training. This University has 3 faculties and 20 departments (courses) that include 12 professional and 8 general subjected departments."@en .
