<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oak_Ridge,_Tennessee> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Oak Ridge** is a city in [Anderson](:Anderson_County%2C_Tennessee) and [Roane](:Roane_County%2C_Tennessee) counties in the [eastern part](:East_Tennessee) of the [U.S. state](:U%2ES%2E_state) of [Tennessee](:Tennessee), about 25 miles (40 km) west of downtown [Knoxville](:Knoxville%2C_Tennessee). Oak Ridge's population was 31,402 at the 2020 census. It is part of the [Knoxville Metropolitan Area](:Knoxville_Metropolitan_Area). Oak Ridge's nicknames include *the Atomic City*, *the Secret City*, *the Ridge*, *the Town the Atomic Bomb Built*, and *the City Behind the Fence*.In 1942, the United States federal government purchased nearly 60,000 acres of farmland in the [Clinch River](:Clinch_River) Valley for the development of a [planned city](:Planned_community) supporting 75,000 residents. It was constructed with assistance from architectural and engineering firm [Skidmore, Owings & Merrill](:Skidmore%2C_Owings_%26_Merrill), from 1942 to 1943. Oak Ridge was established in 1942 as a production site for the [Manhattan Project](:Manhattan_Project)—the massive American, British, and Canadian operation that developed the [atomic bomb](:Nuclear_weapon). Being the site of [Oak Ridge National Laboratory](:Oak_Ridge_National_Laboratory) and [Y-12 National Security Complex](:Y-12_National_Security_Complex), scientific and technological development still plays a crucial role in the city's economy and culture in general."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
