<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tatebayashi,_Gunma> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Tatebayashi** (館林市, *Tatebayashi-shi*) is a [city](:Cities_of_Japan) located in [Gunma Prefecture](:Gunma_Prefecture), Japan. As of 1 September 2020[[update]](//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Tatebayashi,_Gunma&action=edit), the city had an estimated [population](:Population) of 75,442 in 33,589 households, and a [population density](:Population_density) of 1200 people per km². The total area of the city is 60.97 square kilometres (23.54 sq mi). Tatebayashi is famous for Azalea Hill Park and [Bunbuku Chagama](:Bunbuku_Chagama) of Morin-ji temple."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
