<http://dbpedia.org/resource/McGill_University> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**McGill University** (Template:Lang-fr is an English-language [public](:Public_university) [research university](:Research_university) located in [Montreal, Quebec](:Montreal%2C_Quebec), [Canada](:Canada). Founded in 1821 by [royal charter](:Royal_charter) granted by [King George IV](:George_IV), the university bears the name of [James McGill](:James_McGill), a Scottish merchant whose [bequest](:Bequest) in 1813 formed the university's precursor, University of McGill College (or simply, McGill College); the name was officially changed to McGill University in 1885.McGill's main campus is on the slope of [Mount Royal](:Mount_Royal) in [downtown Montreal](:Downtown_Montreal) in the borough of [Ville-Marie](:Ville-Marie%2C_Montreal), with a [second campus](:Macdonald_Campus) situated in [Sainte-Anne-de-Bellevue](:Sainte-Anne-de-Bellevue%2C_Quebec), 30 kilometres (19 mi) west of the main campus on Montreal Island. The university is one of two members of the [Association of American Universities](:Association_of_American_Universities) located outside the United States, alongside the [University of Toronto](:University_of_Toronto), and is the only Canadian member of the [Global University Leaders Forum](:Global_University_Leaders_Forum) (GULF) within the [World Economic Forum](:World_Economic_Forum).McGill offers degrees and diplomas in over 300 fields of study, with the highest average entering grades of any Canadian university. Most students are enrolled in the six largest faculties, namely [Arts](:Arts), [Science](:McGill_University_Faculty_of_Science), [Medicine](:McGill_University_Faculty_of_Medicine), [Education](:McGill_University_Faculty_of_Education), [Engineering](:McGill_University_Faculty_of_Engineering), and [Management](:Desautels_Faculty_of_Management). McGill is the most internationally diverse of any medical-doctoral research university in Canada, with international students comprising over 30% of its student population and hailing from more than 150 countries. Additionally, over 41% of students are born outside of Canada. McGill is ranked among the world's top universities by major educational publications, and has held the top position in the country for the past 18 years in the annual *[Maclean's](:Maclean%27s)* [Canadian university rankings](:Rankings_of_universities_in_Canada).McGill counts among its alumni and faculty 12 [Nobel laureates](:List_of_McGill_University_people%23Nobel_Prize_graduates_and_faculty_members) and 147 [Rhodes Scholars](:Rhodes_Scholars), both the most of any university in Canada, as well as 159 [Loran Scholars](:Loran_Scholars_Foundation), 18 billionaires, the [current prime minister](:Justin_Trudeau) and two former [prime ministers of Canada](:List_of_prime_ministers_of_Canada), two [Governors General of Canada](:Governor_General_of_Canada), 15 justices of the [Supreme Court of Canada](:Supreme_Court_of_Canada), at least eight [foreign leaders](:Leader), and more than 100 members of [national legislatures](:List_of_legislatures_by_country). McGill alumni also include 8 [Academy Award](:Academy_Award) winners, 13 [Grammy Award](:Grammy_Award) winners, at least 13 [Emmy Award](:Emmy_Award) winners, four [Pulitzer Prize](:Pulitzer_Prize) winners, and 121 [Olympians](:Olympic_Games) with over 35 [Olympic](:Olympic_Games) medals. The inventors of the game of [basketball](:Basketball), modern organized [ice hockey](:Ice_hockey), and the pioneers of [gridiron football](:Gridiron_football), as well as the founders of several major universities and colleges are also graduates of the university.Notable researchers include [Ernest Rutherford](:Ernest_Rutherford), who discovered the [atomic nucleus](:Atomic_nucleus) and conducted his Nobel Prize–winning research on the nature of [radioactivity](:Radioactivity) while working as Professor of Experimental Physics at the university. Other notable inventions by McGillians include the world's first [artificial cell](:Artificial_cell), [web search engine](:Web_search_engine), and [charge-coupled device](:Charge-coupled_device), among others.McGill has the largest [endowment per student](:List_of_Canadian_universities_by_endowment) with regard to financial endowments of over C$1 billion in Canada. In 2019, it was the recipient of the largest single philanthropic gift in Canadian history, a $200 million donation to fund the creation of the [McCall MacBain](:John_MacBain) Scholarships programme."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
