<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pasadena,_California> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Pasadena** ( [*PAS-ə-DEE-nə*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key%29) is a city in [Los Angeles County, California](:Los_Angeles_County%2C_California), 11 miles (18 km) northeast of [downtown Los Angeles](:Downtown_Los_Angeles). It is the most populous city and the primary cultural center of the [San Gabriel Valley](:San_Gabriel_Valley). [Old Pasadena](:Old_Pasadena) is the city's original commercial district.Its population was 138,699 at the [2020 census](:2020_United_States_Census), making it the [44th largest city](:List_of_cities_and_towns_in_California) in California and the ninth-largest city in Los Angeles County. Pasadena was incorporated on June 19, 1886, becoming one of the first cities to be incorporated in what is now Los Angeles County, following the city of [Los Angeles](:Los_Angeles) (April 4, 1850).Pasadena is known for hosting the annual [Rose Bowl](:Rose_Bowl_Game) [football](:American_football) game and [Tournament of Roses Parade](:Rose_Parade). It is also home to many scientific, educational, and cultural institutions, including [Caltech](:California_Institute_of_Technology), [Pasadena City College](:Pasadena_City_College), [Kaiser Permanente Bernard J. Tyson School of Medicine](:Kaiser_Permanente_Bernard_J%2E_Tyson_School_of_Medicine), [Fuller Theological Seminary](:Fuller_Theological_Seminary), [ArtCenter College of Design](:Art_Center_College_of_Design), the [Pasadena Playhouse](:Pasadena_Playhouse), the [Ambassador Auditorium](:Ambassador_Auditorium), the [Norton Simon Museum](:Norton_Simon_Museum), and the [USC Pacific Asia Museum](:USC_Pacific_Asia_Museum)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
