<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Milton_Orville_Thompson> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Milton Orville Thompson** (May 4, 1926 – August 6, 1993), ([Lt Cmdr](:Lieutenant_Commander_%28United_States%29), [USNR](:United_States_Naval_Reserve%29), better known as **Milt Thompson**, was an American [naval officer](:United_States_Navy), [aviator](:United_States_naval_aviator), [engineer](:Engineer), and [NASA](:NASA) research pilot. He was one of twelve pilots who flew the [North American X-15](:North_American_X-15), an experimental [spaceplane](:Spaceplane) jointly operated by the [United States Air Force](:United_States_Air_Force) and NASA. He was also selected for participation in the [X-20 Dyna-Soar](:X-20_Dyna-Soar) program.Following his involvement with the X-15 program, Thompson became Chief Engineer and Director of Research Projects at the NASA [Dryden Flight Research Center](:Dryden_Flight_Research_Center)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
