<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Space_Shuttle_Challenger_disaster> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Space Shuttle Challenger disaster was a fatal incident on January 28, 1986, in the United States space program where the Space Shuttle Challenger (OV-099) broke apart 73 seconds into its flight, killing all seven crew members aboard. It was the first fatal accident involving an American spacecraft in flight. The mission, designated STS-51-L, was the tenth flight for the orbiter Challenger and the twenty-fifth flight of the Space Shuttle fleet. The crew was scheduled to deploy a communications satellite and study Halley's Comet while they were in orbit, in addition to taking school teacher Christa McAuliffe into space; the latter resulted in schoolchildren and students across the United States watching the disaster live on television. The spacecraft disintegrated 46,000 feet (14 km) abo"@en .
