<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tracy_Caldwell_Dyson> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Tracy Caldwell Dyson** (born **Tracy Ellen Caldwell**; August 14, 1969) is an American [chemist](:Chemist) and [NASA](:NASA) [astronaut](:Astronaut). Caldwell Dyson was a Mission Specialist on [Space Shuttle](:Space_Shuttle) [*Endeavour*](:Space_Shuttle_Endeavour) flight [STS-118](:STS-118) in August 2007 and part of the [Expedition 23](:Expedition_23) and [Expedition 24](:Expedition_24) crew on the [International Space Station](:International_Space_Station) from April 2010 to September 2010. She has completed three spacewalks, logging more than 22 hrs of [EVA](:Extra-vehicular_activity)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
