<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Aktobe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Aktobe (Kazakh: Ақтөбе, romanized: Aqtöbe; Russian: Актобе, romanized: Aktobe) is a city on the Ilek River in Kazakhstan. It is the administrative center of Aktobe Region. In 2020, it had a population of 500,757 people. Aktobe is located in the west of Kazakhstan. The area of the city is about 428,469 km2. There are two water reservoirs: Aktobe and Sazdy."@en .
