<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Temple,_Texas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Temple** is a [city](:City) in [Bell County, Texas](:Bell_County%2C_Texas), United States. As of 2020, the city has a population of 82,073 according to the U.S. census, and is one of the two principal cities in Bell County.Located near the [county seat](:County_seat) of [Belton](:Belton%2C_Texas), Temple lies in the region referred to as [Central Texas](:Central_Texas) and is a principal city in the [Killeen–Temple–Fort Hood metropolitan area](:Killeen%E2%80%93Temple%E2%80%93Fort_Hood_metropolitan_area), which as of 2015 had a population of 450,051. Located off [Interstate 35](:Interstate_35), Temple is 65 miles north of [Austin](:Austin%2C_Texas), 34 miles south of [Waco](:Waco%2C_Texas) and 27 miles east of Killeen.The primary economic drivers are the extensive medical community (mostly due to [Baylor Scott & White Medical Center – Temple](:Baylor_Scott_%26_White_Medical_Center_%E2%80%93_Temple%29) and goods distribution based on its central location between the Dallas-Fort Worth, San Antonio, and Houston metropolitan areas, and proximity to larger neighbors Austin and Waco."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
