<http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States_Naval_Academy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **United States Naval Academy** (**US Naval Academy**, **USNA**, or **Navy**) is a [federal service academy](:United_States_Service_academies) in [Annapolis](:Annapolis), [Maryland](:Maryland). It was established on 10 October 1845 during the tenure of [George Bancroft](:George_Bancroft) as [Secretary of the Navy](:Secretary_of_the_Navy). The Naval Academy is the second oldest of the five [U.S. service academies](:United_States_service_academies) and it educates midshipmen for service in the officer corps of the [United States Navy](:United_States_Navy) and [United States Marine Corps](:United_States_Marine_Corps). The 338-acre (137 ha) campus is located on the former grounds of [Fort Severn](:Fort_Severn) at the confluence of the [Severn River](:Severn_River_%28Maryland%29) and [Chesapeake Bay](:Chesapeake_Bay) in [Anne Arundel County](:Anne_Arundel_County%2C_Maryland), 33 miles (53 km) east of Washington, D.C., and 26 miles (42 km) southeast of [Baltimore](:Baltimore). The entire campus (known to insiders as \"the Yard\") is a [National Historic Landmark](:National_Historic_Landmark) and home to many historic sites, buildings, and monuments. It replaced [Philadelphia Naval Asylum](:Philadelphia_Naval_Asylum), in [Philadelphia](:Philadelphia), that had served as the first United States Naval Academy from 1838 to 1845, when the Naval Academy formed in Annapolis.Candidates for admission generally must apply directly to the academy and apply separately for a nomination, usually from a [member of Congress](:United_States_Congress). Students are officers-in-training with the rank of [midshipman](:Midshipman). Tuition for midshipmen is fully funded by the Navy in exchange for an active duty service obligation upon graduation. Approximately 1,200 \"plebes\" (an abbreviation of the Ancient Roman word *[plebeian](:Plebeian)*) enter the academy each summer for the rigorous [Plebe Summer](:Plebe_Summer). About 1,000 midshipmen graduate. Graduates are [commissioned](:Commissioned_officer) as either [ensigns](:Ensign_%28rank%29) in the Navy or [second lieutenants](:Second_lieutenant) in the Marine Corps, but a small number can also be cross-commissioned as officers in other U.S. services, and the services of allied nations. The United States Naval Academy has some of the highest paid graduates in the country according to starting salary. The academic program grants a Bachelor of Science degree with a curriculum that grades midshipmen's performance upon a broad academic program, military leadership performance, and mandatory participation in competitive athletics. Midshipmen are required to adhere to the academy's [Honor Concept](:Honor_Concept)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
