<http://dbpedia.org/resource/California_Polytechnic_State_University,_San_Luis_Obispo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**California Polytechnic State University, San Luis Obispo** (**California Polytechnic State University**, **Cal Poly** or **Cal Poly San Luis Obispo**,) is a [public university](:Public_university) in [San Luis Obispo County](:San_Luis_Obispo_County), located directly adjacent to the City of [San Luis Obispo](:San_Luis_Obispo). It is the oldest of [three polytechnics](:Cal_Poly_%28disambiguation%29) in the [California State University](:California_State_University) system.The university is organized into six colleges offering 65 [bachelor's](:Bachelor%27s_degrees) and 39 [master's degrees](:Master%27s_degrees). Cal Poly San Luis Obispo primarily focuses on undergraduate education and as of fall 2020, Cal Poly had 21,447 undergraduate and 840 graduate students. The academic focus is on combining technical and professional curriculums with the arts and humanities. Most of the university's athletic teams participate in the [Big West Conference](:Big_West_Conference). Cal Poly is eligible to be designated as an [Asian American Native American Pacific Islander serving institution](:Minority-serving_institution) (AANAPISI)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
