<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Guion_Bluford> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Guion Stewart Bluford Jr.** (born November 22, 1942) is an American [aerospace engineer](:Aerospace_engineer), retired [United States Air Force](:United_States_Air_Force) (USAF) officer and [fighter pilot](:Fighter_pilot), and former [NASA](:NASA) [astronaut](:Astronaut) in which capacity he became the second [person of African descent](:Black_people) to go to [space](:Outer_space). While assigned to NASA, he remained a USAF officer rising to the rank of [colonel](:Colonel_%28United_States%29). He participated in four [Space Shuttle](:Space_Shuttle) flights between 1983 and 1992. In 1983, as a member of the crew of the Orbiter [*Challenger*](:Space_Shuttle_Challenger) on the mission [STS-8](:STS-8), he became the first African American in space as well as the second [person of African descent](:Black_people) in space, after Cuban cosmonaut [Arnaldo Tamayo Méndez](:Arnaldo_Tamayo_M%C3%A9ndez)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
