<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ilan_Ramon> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Ilan Ramon** (Template:Lang-he; Template:IPA-he, born **Ilan Wolfferman** אילן וולפרמן; June 20, 1954 – February 1, 2003) was an [Israeli](:Israel) fighter pilot and later the first Israeli [astronaut](:Astronaut). Ramon was a [Space Shuttle](:Space_Shuttle) payload specialist of [STS-107](:STS-107), the fatal mission of *[Columbia](:Space_Shuttle_Columbia)*, in which he and the six other crew members were killed when the spacecraft [disintegrated during re-entry](:Space_Shuttle_Columbia_disaster). At 48, he was the oldest member of the crew. Ramon is the only foreign recipient of the United States [Congressional Space Medal of Honor](:Congressional_Space_Medal_of_Honor), which he was awarded posthumously."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
