<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pierre_J._Thuot> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Pierre Joseph Thuot (/ˈθuːət/; born May 19, 1955) is a retired United States Navy captain and NASA astronaut. He went into space three times, spending over 650 hours in space, including over 15 hours in three space walks. He is a former U.S. record holder for time spent on one spacewalk, and participated in the first three-person spacewalk."@en .
