<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ernst_Messerschmid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Ernst Willi Messerschmid** (born 21 May 1945) is a German physicist and former [astronaut](:Astronaut).Born in [Reutlingen](:Reutlingen), Germany, Messerschmid finished the *Technisches Gymnasium* in [Stuttgart](:Stuttgart) in 1965. After two years of military service he studied physics at the [University of Tübingen](:University_of_T%C3%BCbingen) and [Bonn](:University_of_Bonn), receiving a [Diplom](:Diplom) degree in 1972 and doctorate in 1976. From 1970 to 1975 he was also a visiting scientist at the [CERN](:CERN) in [Geneva](:Geneva), working on [proton beams](:Charged_particle_beam) in accelerators and plasmas. From 1975 to 1976 he worked at the [University of Freiburg](:University_of_Freiburg) and the [Brookhaven National Laboratory](:Brookhaven_National_Laboratory) (New York), In 1977, he joined [DESY](:DESY) in [Hamburg](:Hamburg) to work on the beam optics of the PETRA storage ring.From 1978 to 1982, he worked at the [DFVLR](:DFVLR) (the precursor of the [DLR](:German_Aerospace_Center%29) in the Institute of Communications Technology in [Oberpfaffenhofen](:Oberpfaffenhofen) on space-borne communications. In 1983, he was selected as one of the astronauts for the first German [Spacelab](:Spacelab) mission D-1. He flew as a payload specialist on [STS-61-A](:STS-61-A) in 1985, spending over 168 hours in space.After his spaceflight he became a professor at the *Institut für Raumfahrtsysteme* at the [University of Stuttgart](:University_of_Stuttgart). From 2000 to 2004, he was head of the [European Astronaut Centre](:European_Astronaut_Centre) in [Cologne](:Cologne). In January 2005, he returned to the University of Stuttgart teaching on subjects of Astronautics and Space Stations."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
