<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Svitlovodsk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Svitlovodsk (Ukrainian: Світлово́дськ, translit. Svitlovóds’k, Russian: Светловодск) is a city in central Ukraine located on the Dnieper River in Oleksandriia Raion, Kirovohrad Oblast. It hosts the administration of , one of the hromadas of Ukraine. Its population is approximately 43,931 (2021 est.). In 1962–1969, the city carried the name Kremhes due to the fact that it is a city-satellite of Kremenchuk."@en .
