<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Jean-Pierre_Haigneré> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Jean-Pierre Haigneré** (born 19 May 1948) is a [French Air Force](:French_Air_Force) officer and a former [CNES](:CNES) [spationaut](:Spationaut).Jean-Pierre Haigneré was born in [Paris](:Paris), France, and joined the French Air Force, where he trained as a test pilot.He flew on two missions to the [Mir](:Mir) space station in 1993 and 1999. The [Mir Perseus (Mir EO-27)](:List_of_Mir_Expeditions) long-duration mission (186 days) in 1999 also included an [EVA](:Extra-vehicular_activity).In addition to his duties at the [European Space Agency](:European_Space_Agency), Jean-Pierre Haigneré is also involved in a European [space tourism](:Space_tourism) initiative, the *[Astronaute Club Européen](:Astronaute_Club_Europ%C3%A9en)* (ACE), which he co-founded with Alain Dupas and Laurent Gathier."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
