<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Riga> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Riga (/ˈriːɡə/; Latvian: Rīga [ˈriːɡa], Livonian: Rīgõ) is the capital and largest city of Latvia and is home to 671,000 inhabitants which is a third of Latvia's population. It is also the largest city in the three Baltic states and is home to one tenth of the three Baltic states' combined population. The city lies on the Gulf of Riga at the mouth of the Daugava river where it meets the Baltic Sea. Riga's territory covers 307.17 km2 (118.60 sq mi) and lies 1–10 m (3.3–32.8 ft) above sea level, on a flat and sandy plain."@en .
