<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bob_Behnken> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Robert Louis Behnken** (; born July 28, 1970, in [St. Ann, Missouri](:St%2E_Ann%2C_Missouri%29) is a [NASA](:NASA) [astronaut](:Astronaut), [engineer](:Engineer), and former [Chief of the Astronaut Office](:Chief_of_the_Astronaut_Office). Behnken holds a [Ph.D](:Ph%2ED) in [mechanical engineering](:Mechanical_engineering) and the rank of [colonel](:Colonel_%28United_States%29) in the U.S. Air Force, where he served before joining NASA in 2000. He flew aboard [Space Shuttle](:Space_Shuttle) missions [STS-123](:STS-123) (2008) and [STS-130](:STS-130) (2010) as a [mission specialist](:Mission_specialist), accumulating over 708 hours in space, including 55 hours of [spacewalk](:Spacewalk) time. He is married to fellow astronaut [K. Megan McArthur](:K%2E_Megan_McArthur).Following retirement of the Space Shuttle, Behnken was [Chief of the Astronaut Office](:Chief_of_the_Astronaut_Office) from 2012 to 2015. Assigned to the [SpaceX](:SpaceX) [Dragon Capsule](:Dragon_Capsule) in 2018 as part of NASA's [Commercial Crew Program](:Commercial_Crew_Program), Behnken launched aboard the spacecraft's first crewed mission with fellow astronaut [Doug Hurley](:Doug_Hurley) on May 30, 2020, and became one of the first two astronauts launching aboard a commercial orbital spacecraft in spaceflight history. The mission, [Crew Dragon Demo-2](:Crew_Dragon_Demo-2), took Behnken and Hurley to the [International Space Station](:International_Space_Station) (ISS), where they docked and stayed aboard for 62 days. Behnken completed four spacewalks with NASA Astronaut [Christopher Cassidy](:Christopher_Cassidy)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
