<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Gerald_Carr_(astronaut)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "[Colonel](:Colonel_%28United_States%29) **Gerald Paul Carr** (August 22, 1932 – August 26, 2020) was an American [mechanical](:Mechanical_engineering) and [aeronautical engineer](:Aeronautical_engineer), [United States Marine Corps officer](:United_States_Marine_Corps), [naval aviator](:Naval_aviator), and [NASA](:NASA) [astronaut](:Astronaut). He was Commander of [Skylab 4](:Skylab_4), the third and final crewed visit to the [Skylab Orbital Workshop](:Skylab), from November 16, 1973, to February 8, 1974."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Expedition_39> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expedition 39 was the 39th expedition to the International Space Station. It marked the first time the ISS had been under command of a Japanese astronaut, space veteran Koichi Wakata. After Expedition 21 in 2009 and Expedition 35 in 2013, it was only the third time an ISS crew was led by neither a NASA nor an RSA crew member. During Expedition 39, Astronauts Mastracchio and Swanson installed the \"Veggie\" project on the International Space Station."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Latvia> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/giniCoefficient> "35.7"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Province_of_Maryland> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Country> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Richard_Mastracchio> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Richard Alan \"Rick\" Mastracchio** (born February 11, 1960) is an American [engineer](:Engineer) and former [NASA](:NASA) [astronaut](:Astronaut). He has flown on three NASA Space Shuttle missions as a [mission specialist](:Mission_specialist) in addition to serving as a Flight Engineer on the [Soyuz TMA-11M](:Soyuz_TMA-11M) ([Expedition 38](:Expedition_38)/[Expedition 39](:Expedition_39%29) long duration mission aboard the [International Space Station](:International_Space_Station). He is currently the Senior Director of Operations for Commercial Resupply Services at [Orbital ATK](:Orbital_ATK)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Crookston,_Minnesota> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Crookston** is a city in the [U.S. state](:U%2ES%2E_state) of [Minnesota](:Minnesota). It is the [county seat](:County_seat) of [Polk County](:Polk_County%2C_Minnesota). The population was 7,482 at the [2020 census](:2020_United_States_census). It is part of the \"[Grand Forks](:Grand_Forks%2C_North_Dakota), [ND](:North_Dakota)-[MN](:Minnesota) [Metropolitan Statistical Area](:Metropolitan_Statistical_Area)\" or \"[Greater Grand Forks](:Greater_Grand_Forks)\".Crookston is the [episcopal seat](:Episcopal_seat) of the [Roman Catholic Diocese of Crookston](:Roman_Catholic_Diocese_of_Crookston). Crookston is partially a commuter town to the larger city of [Grand Forks, North Dakota](:Grand_Forks%2C_North_Dakota)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
